the russian ministry of defence says  this destroyed building was a ukrainian  weapons factory in the southwest  outskirts of the capital kiev  moscow says the plant made anti-aircraft  and anti-ship missiles people living  nearby say they heard at least three  large explosions early friday morning  we parked the car and the two rockets  hit at 1am i did not realize that there  are two rockets coming in but when i  went out afterwards i waited indoors for  some time fearing more shelling we saw  the third one coming it damaged the car  tore out the tires hit the windows and  walls people suffered too the walls fell  the out came hours after russia said its  black sea fleet flagship the mosque bar  had sunk while being towed back to port  after a fire caused an explosion on  board  ukrainian military said it was  responsible having targeted the vessel  with ukrainian-made neptune missiles  people gathered at a memorial ceremony  for the ship in the port city of  sevastopol in russian annexed crimea  the moskva was the largest russian naval  vessel to have sunk in action since  world war ii  even for those who have not been there  moskva was a symbol for everyone symbol  of our power our hope the revival of the  fleet in the 90s it is a symbol of  engineering and scientific achievements  force of our arms  the ukrainian army says it repelled  russian army advances on at least two  towns in the east of the country  russia has redirected its forces from  kiev in an effort to seize more  territory in the donbass region  volunteers help ukrainian soldiers pack  food to be distributed to some of the  many thousands of people fleeing all  those still living in the worst affected  areas i stay here because it's my home  and we help people delivering food  chemistry  and  our  town  just destroying  oh it's not good  i don't know what to say  okay i want to move  okay this drone footage shows destroyed  residential buildings in mariopol  the besieged port city on the azov sea  has suffered seven weeks of bombardment  by russian forces and pro-russian  separatists  repeated attempts at securing  humanitarian corridors to rescue  thousands of people trapped inside have  failed  the mayor of the city estimates  thousands of civilians may have been  killed in the fighting  ukraine's ministry of defense says  russia has for the first time used  long-range bombers to attack the city  russian occupants keep carrying out  aerial strikes on mariopol they use  long-range bombers the enemy's land  forces are trying to capture the seaport  the strike on what the russian defense  ministry describes as a weapons factory  on the outskirts of kiev is the first  major strike by russian forces on a  target around the capital city  since russian forces left the area more  than two weeks ago  major military operations now for the  time being have moved east where there  are increasing reports of an effort by  the russian military to close in  around the strategically important city  of slavyansk  the un says that more than 4.7 million  people have fled the fighting and with  no  indication of any de-escalation that  number is expected to rise charles  stratford al jazeera kiev
 

